README.md:16:The generator composes the paper's necklace graphs `N_r`. Each necklace is made from copies of `K4-e` joined through their degree-two vertices (Theorem 2.13 and Lemma 2.14). Remark 2.12 gives the executable obstruction: the two non-connector vertices in each diamond are true twins, so a size-`r` power dominating set must meet all `r` diamonds. Conversely, any one vertex per diamond works. Generation samples those representatives first and only then relabels the graph; it never solves the generated instance.
