/tmp/tmp.e6ZuziTSpx/NGpowerdomination_nolinenumbers.tex:416:Necessarily, $n$ is a multiple of 3 and $n\ne 3$.  If $G$ has 2 or more components, then $\gamma(\Gc)\le 2$ by Theorem \ref{diam3+}.  If $G=K_{3,3}$, then $\pd(\Gc)=2$.  Now suppose $G$ has a component $G_o\in \maxpd$ of order at least $6$ (this includes the case where $G$ has only one component that is not $K_{3,3}$).  Then $\pd(\overline{G_o})=1$ by Lemma \ref{foliatecomplem} and  Proposition \ref{GBarBd1} (for the case $v''\not\in N(v')$).  In $\Gc$, any vertex in $G_o$ dominates any vertex in a different component, so the one vertex that power dominates $\overline{G_o}$ also power dominates $\Gc$, and  $\pd(\Gc)=1$.  \end{proof}
